<!--
  Opendoor "Time Track Highlight" -> knocking. Hourly, 8am-10pm.

  Same cadence as before — hourly — just starting at 8am instead of 2pm, so the
  board is current from the start of the day rather than only from mid-afternoon.
  ~15 runs a day against ~10 before.

  The one structural change: StartInterval, like the sr-sync and amplify-sync
  agents, with the window enforced inside run-rtr-sync.sh (RTR_START_HOUR /
  RTR_END_HOUR) instead of a list of calendar hours. This is a laptop, and
  StartCalendarInterval firings missed while the lid is shut are DROPPED, not
  queued — which is how the board could sit hours stale with no run to fix it.
  launchd coalesces missed StartInterval firings into one catch-up run on wake,
  and since the report is cumulative for the day that single run restores the
  whole day.

  Cost is worth knowing since this renders a report on Opendoor's SSRS server
  rather than hitting a JSON API. Every 30 min across the 8am-10pm window is ~28
  renders a day per ISP, up from ~15 hourly. That was a deliberate stopping
  point: the report is CUMULATIVE for the day, so cadence buys smoothness, not
  correctness — hourly made a rep's doors climb in visible steps (49 -> 135 ->
  303 -> 526 on 2026-08-07) and 30 min halves that. Going to 10 min would be ~84
  Chrome renders a day against someone else's reporting box for very little
  more, so it was considered and declined.

  To change it, edit StartInterval below (1800 = every 30 min) or the hours in
  run-rtr-sync.sh, and the `every:` / `sched:` values on the 'rtr' row in
  index.html (_growSyncStatus) so the health board stays honest.

  Outside the window the script exits immediately without touching Chrome or
  Opendoor, so off-hours ticks cost nothing.

  Sealing yesterday: unchanged, and NOT pinned to an hour. The runner seals on
  the first successful run of each day, tracked by imports/done/rtr-last-sealed,
  which with this window is the ~8am run. Reps' phones sync to SalesRabbit after
  they stop knocking, so that morning re-pull is what makes yesterday final.

  Install:
    cp scripts/launchd/com.grow.rtr-sync.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.grow.rtr-sync.plist 2>/dev/null
    launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.grow.rtr-sync.plist
  Check:   launchctl list | grep rtr-sync
  Remove:  launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.grow.rtr-sync.plist

  FIRST: node scripts/rtr-sync.mjs --login   (a window opens; sign in once)
-->
